WEBVTT

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:40.250
Wow, Joe is living in a pretty nice place.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.520
You idiot! He's not living here.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.400
He's being held here.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.290
Hey, hey, be quiet!

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.290
Now listen, Joe doesn't have a proper guardian.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:54.250
That's how I managed to call in a special favor so you guys could see him.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.630
So be quiet!

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.460
That's true.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.530
If we're noisy and they decide that Joe must be a delinquent, then...

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.210
That's right, Sachi.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.780
Joe's fate will depend on the judge's impression of him.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.860
Joe's fate will depend on the judge's impression of him.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.610
What do you mean, impression?

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:18.100
In other words, we need the court to like us.

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.040
Okay, leave it to me!

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.620
Hey, just a moment, just a moment!

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.460
Thank you very much!

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.530
I'm very sorry that Joe has caused you so much trouble!

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.760
I'm very sorry that Joe has caused you so much trouble!

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:47.170
I'm very sorry that Joe caused so much trouble!

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:48.930
That idiot, what is he doing?

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:51.890
Hey, Kinoko! Just sit down and be quiet!

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:54.640
But boss, we have to make a good impression!

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.340
What are you talking about!? Do you think that will make a good impression?

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.840
Making a fuss now won't change anything.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.950
There's no way he'll be released.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:05.770
So Joe will be put away for another month or two?

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:08.950
There's no way he'll only get one or two months, you guys!

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:14.480
After all, he committed such a terrible crime.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.980
Worst case scenario, he'll get one year and one month.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.880
Yabuki-kun will probably get sent to a special juvenile detention center.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.040
One year and one month!

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.810
Special

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.890
juvenile detention center?

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.390
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:40.360
What!? Stop saying that stuff! It hasn't been decided yet!

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:40.740
Wait, wait.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.780
Calm down, Sachi.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:46.740
Miss, please forgive us.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:51.750
Everyone's been so worried about Joe, they just...

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.320
We will now begin Yabuki Joe's hearing.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.720
Everyone, please make your way into the courtroom.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.230
If you make too much noise, you'll be asked to leave.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:36.040
That whistling! It's the boss!

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:37.500
It's Joe!

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.590
Boss!

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.050
Hey!

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.260
Stop whistling!

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.880
Stop it, I said!

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.290
Yabuki!

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:46.110
Stop it!

00:04:59.120 --> 00:04:59.870
Joe!

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:00.570
Boss!

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.510
Yo,

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:05.150
you're all here!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.270
What's this?

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.240
You all look awfully sad to see me!

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:11.560
Joe,

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.840
if you aren't good, you'll make a bad impression.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:15.870
Impression?

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.690
You're worried about me.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:21.790
Don't worry!

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:23.920
I'll be good.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:25.840
Really?

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.760
Yeah, I won't make you worry.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.490
Yabuki, take the stand.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:32.470
Shut up, I got it!

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:35.910
Joe,

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.480
you look well.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:42.970
Everyone was worried about you.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:50.620
So you read "For the Sake of Tomorrow #1," right?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.620
I read it very carefully.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.210
Do you want to test out my left jab, old man?

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.040
What's the matter? Come on down.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:34.080
Stand!

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:39.300
Be seated.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:48.690
I will now read the charges against the youth, Yabuki Joe.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:55.680
Yabuki, what are you looking at!?

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.350
Face forward! Forward!

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.900
First, can we get rid of this white rat that's snuck in?

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:06.320
Having it running around gets on my nerves.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:09.220
Yabuki, face forward already.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:10.150
Shut up!

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:13.660
I said to get rid of her! Do you understand, you pig?

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.070
Old man...

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:21.370
Yabuki, you don't have the right to choose your audience.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.090
Wait a second, boss man!

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.710
Who do you think gives you your jobs?

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.890
The only reason you get to be smug up there is because there are bad guys like us!

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.390
Joe, what are you saying!?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:37.350
Joe, you stupid idiot!

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:37.940
Stupid!

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:39.430
Stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid!

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:40.890
STUPID!

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:44.900
Stop it Sachi! Stop it! Sachi! Stop!

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:44.900
Let me go! Let me go! Let me go! Let me go!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.900
Stupid idiot! Joe is a stupid liar!

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:52.770
No matter how good we are,

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.410
if Joe is like that...

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.270
Order! Order!

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:04.410
If there are any more outbursts, everyone will be kicked out.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:06.050
Be quiet.

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:13.250
Hey, judge guy,

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:16.990
why don't we finish this before any more sandals are thrown at me?

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:25.430
When Yabuki Joe was young,

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:28.040
his parents abandoned him.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:31.990
We must be sympathetic to this situation.

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:36.590
Like many other young children without parents,

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:41.910
he was put into a difficult situation at an early age.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:58.260
<i>READY!</i>

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.100
<i>Joe, where are you running!?</i>

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.610
<i>Wait a minute! He's escaping!</i>

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:19.150
<i>Idiots!</i>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.520
<i>Ouch!</i>

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:43.110
<i>Hey,</i>

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:44.470
<i>something is wrong!</i>

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:45.980
<i>What?</i>

00:09:54.560 --> 00:10:04.490
Escape after escape, he made his way from Hokkaido to Kyushu without settling down.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:09.020
His entire youth was spent wandering from place to place.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:14.170
From this, we can understand his character.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:15.920
Nice! Very nice!

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.400
That was impressive.

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:21.850
Even if it's your job, that was very well researched. I'm impressed.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.750
Anyhow, let's get on with it.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.020
Move on, please.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:29.520
Stupid!

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.170
Joe...

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:42.520
Finally, he ended up coming to Tokyo, enlisted those children as his subordinates,

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:45.880
and engaged in delinquency such as the incident in question.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:53.500
He manipulated the media and caused an incident in which many people were deceived.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:11:02.410
His homeless friend, Tange Danpei, was another drifter who met Yabuki and took him under his wing.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:08.790
He got a job and sacrificed his time to try to teach Yabuki Joe boxing and help him rehabilitate.

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:16.050
Yabuki Joe appeared to be touched by Tange's passion and it seemed he was training hard.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:19.960
However, he betrayed Tange's kindness, and furthermore...

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:06.320
Order!

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.780
Order in the court!

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:44.020
Tange's kindness, you say?

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:45.700
Rehabilitate?

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:49.470
You've got to be kidding.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:51.850
This trial is a waste of time.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:52.750
Yabuki!

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.510
What do you mean, "a waste of time"?

00:12:55.510 --> 00:12:57.290
Well it is, isn't it, old man?

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.000
Right?

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:02.610
After all, no matter how you look at it,

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:05.710
you don't look like you care for kindness or rehabilitation.

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.250
Besides,

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:12.490
you just tried to teach me boxing because I looked strong.

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:13.820
Basically,

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:17.020
you just tried to teach me like a circus trainer teaches a monkey!

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.960
Now, in court, they say it was kindness?

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:21.480
Rehabilitation?

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:23.620
QUIET! {judge}

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:24.990
JOE! {danpe}

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:28.040
You hit the nail right on the head, Joe.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:33.490
I tried to teach you boxing and make money off you!

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:35.830
Old man...

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:37.330
Old man...

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:43.700
I like that pliancy, old man.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:51.270
But, Joe, I have to admit, it wasn't all about the money.

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:53.000
I like the fighting,

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.060
and I also fell for your two arms.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:14:01.810
What made me want to quit being an alcoholic and to start working my ass off

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:07.530
was because I wanted to make you Japan's best-
no, the world's best boxer.

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:11.740
If it's for that, I can even throw away my own life!

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.530
Do you understand!?

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:15.540
That's disgraceful, old man!

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:18.670
Just because you couldn't be Japan's best,

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:20.890
you want me to carry on your dreams?

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:23.040
You're trying to make me your doll, aren't ya!?

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.030
Stop joking around!

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:27.550
I have no time for old men like you!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.820
Order in the court! Order in the Court!

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:38.220
You may only talk after I have given you permission.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:44.770
Now, I would like to present to you the verdict.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:54.710
The verdict:

00:14:54.710 --> 00:15:03.290
Yabuki Joe is sentenced to one year and one month at the Noguki Island Special Juvenile Detention Center!

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.530
Hey, go.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:33.070
Hey, you.

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:36.990
Well, well, Ms. Princess, are you satisfied now?

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:41.950
Are you satisfied seeing me like this now?

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.820
Why don't you say something!?

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:46.170
Staring at me like that!

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:48.980
Yabuki! Stop your yabbering! Go!

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:52.830
The little angel couldn't make a scene this time!

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:53.760
Serves you right!

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.760
What a sad little person.

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:58.550
What!?

00:15:58.550 --> 00:15:59.640
SAY THAT AGAIN!

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:01.270
Now come along.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:03.270
IDIOT!

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.020
Living with lots of money...

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:12.690
When you see a poor person all you say is "what a sad little person" and people call you a princess, an angel of the streets.

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:13.910
Don't make me laugh!

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:15.990
Joe!

00:16:18.090 --> 00:16:19.450
What's this?

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.330
Now it's Daddy Danpei.

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:22.960
You...

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:26.160
While you were gone, you've really become cold.

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:26.980
Look...

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:30.750
Tarou, Sachi, and Kinoko are even frightened.

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:35.500
What, what? You guys look like you're dead!

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:37.010
See me off with a smile.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:41.020
Well, that doesn't really matter now.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.270
Just don't forget the fighting!

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:46.880
Let's go!

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:47.900
The bus is waiting, right?

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:56.830
Joe!

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:59.450
Even if today might be a miserable day for you,

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.080
tomorrow will exist as long as you don't forget about fighting!

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:07.080
Your talent in fighting will wash all of your sins completely away!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:09.260
Got it, Joe?

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.480
For tomorrow!

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:11.720
For tomorrow!

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.120
Quit it, dude!

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:16.700
I'm gone for a year!

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.230
What do you mean, "tomorrow"?

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:19.470
What do you mean, "wash my sins away"!?

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:24.720
Hey, stop making a scene! Get in the car! Hey!

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:27.090
Don't push me! Don't push me, bastard!

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:31.750
C'mon, start the car already.

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:45.670
Joe!

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.910
Joe!

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.270
Boss Joe!

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.610
Boss!

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:01.930
Joe...

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:08.150
Hey! Come back soon!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:09.940
We're waiting!

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:15.960
What are you doing, Sachi?

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:18.510
That's far!

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:21.110
What is?

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:23.420
What is, Sachi?

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:32.130
From here to there! It's 395 tiles away!

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.790
Wow, you're bored.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.020
Did you lose a screw up here?

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:37.060
Idiot!

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:40.050
One year and one month is 395 days!

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:42.530
I get it! Those sandals over there are Joe-niichan's!

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.580
That's far away.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:44.750
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.240
Hey,

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:51.930
it's only a small part of Joe's life.

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:56.230
His life will go on forever, just like this road.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:59.000
On and on, it will continue.

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:01.840
I wonder how Joe-nii is doing.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.840
He's probably on the boat to Nogiku Island.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.960
Hey, Yabuki.

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:39.430
How long are you going to stand there?

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:41.290
Get inside.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:43.970
Shut up. I heard you already.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:46.510
Stay quiet in there, you hear me?

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.000
Who are you?

00:20:55.570 --> 00:20:56.980
Is anyone over there?

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.110
Yo.

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:05.680
You're... Nishi.

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:06.390
You're... Nishi.

00:21:09.190 --> 00:21:12.080
I thought I'd see you again, so I waited here.

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:14.110
Waited here?

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:19.090
Waited here to finish our fight?

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:20.090
I'll be glad to fight you.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:23.250
W-Wait! Don't get it wrong!

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:24.130
Not that!

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:27.490
I'm sick and tired of your fighting!

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:30.950
What I meant was...

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:34.680
Nishi, are you okay?

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:35.760
You're shivering.

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:36.600
You cold?

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:38.450
Joe...

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:39.910
I'm scared...

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:41.610
I'm scared.

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:43.080
Scared?

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:44.110
Of what?

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:46.040
What I'm scared of is

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:50.620
the life at the Special Juvenile Detention Center.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:55.740
What now? What now?

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:58.750
You're big and now you're scared like a little kitty cat!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:00.080
Stop wimping out!

00:22:01.370 --> 00:22:02.000
That's pathetic.

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:06.930
I'm ashamed of you, Nishi.

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:09.010
If I knew that beforehand,

00:22:10.030 --> 00:22:12.550
I shouldn't have bothered with you at the holding facility.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:16.250
You're so lucky,

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:19.520
at least until this ship arrives at Nogiku Island.

00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:25.050
You don't know?

00:22:25.050 --> 00:22:27.030
That place is hell!

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:30.570
People who don't think killing is a sin are walking around.

00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:32.660
For real!

00:22:36.270 --> 00:22:37.770
Quit it!

00:22:37.770 --> 00:22:39.830
I don't know if it's special or quick,

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:42.150
but all they are are a bunch of boys like us.

00:22:42.150 --> 00:22:43.970
This is true. I'm not lying.

00:22:45.530 --> 00:22:46.100
It's true!

00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:52.570
You know, Nishi,

00:22:52.570 --> 00:22:56.100
when I was born, I wasn't given anything a normal boy receives.

00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:58.110
Toys,

00:22:58.110 --> 00:22:59.250
books,

00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:00.860
even warm blankets.

00:23:00.860 --> 00:23:02.140
Nothing.

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:04.860
I didn't even get the proper love from my parents and I live here today,

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:12.040
but I have protected my freedom with my fists.

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:17.580
When my freedom is taken away, what do I have left?

00:23:21.390 --> 00:23:22.930
I'll do it.

00:23:22.930 --> 00:23:24.770
If it's for my freedom,

00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:27.590
even if it's from the pits of hell, I'll get out!

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:44.380
Joe and Nishi have now arrived at the Nogiku Island Special Juvenile Detention Center.

00:23:44.600 --> 00:23:47.620
This is a place where the big waves crash loudly against the reefs.

00:23:47.620 --> 00:23:49.820
There is no way of escaping.

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:53.990
For Joe, who's alone now, which way is tomorrow!?
